{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>And when a ger sojourns with you.</b> Here He agreed to the acceptance of converts from the mixed multitude according to the view of Moses, and this is His saying <b>with you.</b> Further, the supernal Will intimated that it did not agree to the matter except to the desire of Moses — HaShem was willing — as they said, of blessed memory (Exodus Rabbah 42). And this is His saying <b>with you a ger</b> — meaning, with you he is a ger, for you are not versed in what is hidden, and My thoughts are not your thoughts; go out and learn what came to pass at their hands because of them." "<b>Circumcise for him every male.</b> Meaning: just as the circumcision of a slave constitutes a barrier for an Israelite [so that he may not eat of the Paschal offering], so too for the ger, the circumcision of his slaves, etc., constitutes a barrier for him until he circumcises for him every male. And His saying <b>then he may draw near</b> etc. — meaning, it will not be necessary for others to slaughter on his behalf, but he himself may draw near to perform it; <b>and he shall be as a native of the land</b> etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:21.460185017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}